Art
---
This repository contains no art. When it runs, the mod reads the sprites from
the VS Code Pets extension installed on the user's machine, or downloads them
from the VS Code Pets repository. Mirrored copies are made on the user's machine
and are not redistributed. The artists, as credited by VS Code Pets:

- Cat and frog animations: seethingswarm (https://seethingswarm.itch.io)
- Dog media assets: NVPH Studio (https://nvph-studio.itch.io/dog-animation-4-different-dogs),
  licensed CC BY-ND 4.0
- Akita inu: Kevin Huang (https://github.com/kevin2huang)
- Clippy, Rocky, Zappy, rubber duck, snake, cockatiel, Ferris the crab and Mod
  the dotnet bot: Marc Duiker (https://twitter.com/marcduiker)
- Original concept of Ferris the crab: Karen Rustad Tölva (https://www.aldeka.net)
- Fox: Elthen (https://twitter.com/pixelthen)
- Turtle: enkeefe
- Horse: adapted by Chris Kent (https://github.com/thechriskent) from assets by
  Onfe (https://onfe.itch.io/horse-sprite-with-rider-asset-pack)
- Squirrel: adapted by Chris Kent from assets by Azdner (https://azdner.itch.io/)
- Skeleton: adapted by Chris Kent from assets by MonoPixelArt (https://monopixelart.itch.io/)
- Snail: Kennet Shin (https://github.com/WoofWoof0)
- Panda: Jessie Ferris (https://github.com/jeferris)
- Finley: Microsoft Corporation, MIT License
- Winter theme: Kiana Mosser (https://www.instagram.com/kianamosser/)
- Forest theme: edermunizz (https://edermunizz.itch.io/free-pixel-art-forest)
- Castle theme: made with artwork by GuttyKreum (https://guttykreum.itch.io/gothic-castle-game-assets)

See the VS Code Pets README for the full and current credits.
